---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { sitePath } from '../../lib/siteUrl';
import StatusPill from '../../components/StatusPill.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Local Asset Search"
  description="Find design assets by filename, recognized text, tags, description, or an optional local visual query in Varve."
>
  <div class="container-custom">
    <div class="feature-page">
      <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href={sitePath('/features')}>Features</a> / Asset search
      </nav>

      <div class="feature-kicker"><StatusPill status="available" /></div>
      <h1>Find the asset you remember.</h1>
      <p class="feature-intro">
        Search the local asset library using the clue you still have: a description, a filename,
        recognized text, a tag, a path. Varve keeps retrieval inside the asset browser instead of
        turning a simple lookup into a chat session.
      </p>

      <section class="search-demo" aria-label="Asset search example">
        <div class="search-demo__label">Search Assets</div>
        <div class="search-demo__field"><span aria-hidden="true">⌕</span> orange sunset over mountains</div>
        <div class="search-demo__results">
          <span class="search-demo__thumb search-demo__thumb--sunset" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="search-demo__thumb search-demo__thumb--ridge" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="search-demo__thumb search-demo__thumb--poster" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-section">
        <h2>One search, several useful signals</h2>
        <div class="lane-grid">
          <article><h3>Filename and path</h3><p>Exact identifiers such as <code>IMG_4821</code> stay precise.</p></article>
          <article><h3>Recognized text</h3><p>OCR results can surface scans, invoices, and presentation slides.</p></article>
          <article><h3>Tags and metadata</h3><p>Kind, MIME type, descriptions, and user tags remain searchable.</p></article>
          <article><h3>Visual description</h3><p>After the opt-in local model download, the Asset Browser ranks matching images when you describe what you remember — and the Similar panel compares text descriptions with document images.</p></article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-section feature-section--note">
        <h2>Visual search is opt-in and experimental</h2>
        <p>
          The local image/text embedding pair is downloaded only when you ask for it and remains
          inside the app: queries, embeddings, and ranking never leave the device. It is a ranking
          aid—not a quality guarantee—and filename, OCR, tags, and metadata search continue to
          work without the model.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="feature-cta">
        <a href={sitePath('/download')} class="btn-primary">Download Varve</a>
        <a href={sitePath('/docs')} class="btn-secondary">Read the documentation</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .feature-page { max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 3rem 0; }
  .breadcrumb { font-size: 0.875rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .breadcrumb a { color: var(--text-secondary); }
  .feature-kicker { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .feature-page h1 { max-width: 760px; font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4.5rem); line-height: 1.02; font-family: var(--font-editorial); color: var(--text-primary); margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
  .feature-intro { max-width: 700px; font-size: 1.25rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 3rem; }
  .search-demo { padding: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 4rem; border: 1px solid var(--border-default); border-radius: 1rem; background: var(--surface-card); box-shadow: var(--elevation-shadow-raised); }
  .search-demo__label { margin-bottom: 0.6rem; color: var(--text-tertiary); font-size: 0.75rem; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .search-demo__field { padding: 0.9rem 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--border-accent); border-radius: 0.6rem; color: var(--text-primary); font-family: var(--font-mono); }
  .search-demo__field span { margin-right: 0.5rem; color: var(--accent-primary); }
  .search-demo__results { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 0.75rem; margin-top: 1rem; }
  .search-demo__thumb { aspect-ratio: 4 / 3; display: block; border-radius: 0.5rem; }
  .search-demo__thumb--sunset { background: linear-gradient(155deg, #f7b267, #e76f51 48%, #273248 49%, #19202e); }
  .search-demo__thumb--ridge { background: linear-gradient(165deg, #f3a261, #f4d35e 48%, #3d405b 49%, #202337); }
  .search-demo__thumb--poster { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ed6a5a 0 35%, #f4f1de 35% 62%, #3d405b 62%); }
  .feature-section { margin-bottom: 3rem; }
  .feature-section h2 { color: var(--text-primary); font-size: 1.6rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .feature-section p { color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.8; }
  .feature-section--note { border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-primary); padding-left: 1rem; }
  .lane-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 1rem; }
  .lane-grid article { padding: 1.25rem; border: 1px solid var(--border-default); border-radius: 0.7rem; background: var(--surface-card); }
  .lane-grid h3 { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; color: var(--text-primary); font-size: 1rem; }
  .lane-grid p { margin: 0; font-size: 0.95rem; }
  code { color: var(--text-primary); }
  .feature-cta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.75rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--border-default); padding-top: 2rem; }
  .btn-secondary { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; padding: 0.7rem 1.1rem; border: 1px solid var(--border-default); border-radius: 0.5rem; color: var(--text-primary); text-decoration: none; }
  @media (max-width: 680px) { .lane-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
